  "summary": {
    "as": "Reported to House",
    "asOf": "2026-10-09",
    "date": "2026-11-04T17:55:13Z",
    "text": "504 Program Level Flexibility Act\n\nThis bill authorizes the Small Business Administration (SBA), upon a determination that the amount of its commitments to guarantee loans under the 504 Loan Program could exceed the authorized annual limit, to guarantee up to 115% of that limit.\n\nThe 504 Loan Program provides a small business with\u00a0SBA financing\u2014through a certified development company intermediary\u2014for expansion or modernization.\n\nThe bill requires the SBA to notify\u00a0Congress if it intends to use this authority. The SBA may exercise the authority only once each fiscal year."
  },
